# VENTION-SDLC-MANAGED:BEGIN
#
# Everything between BEGIN / END is framework-managed and rewritten on every
# `vsdlc install`. Add your team's ignore rules OUTSIDE these markers — they
# will be preserved byte-for-byte across upgrades.
#
# --- per-developer state (R3 — never committed) -------------------------
/.vsdlc/workspace.local.toml
/.vsdlc/telemetry/
/.vsdlc/.lock
/.mcp.json
/.vscode
/.mise.toml
# --- framework-owned IDE config (R10 watched paths) ---------------------
/.claude/
/.cursor/
/.codex/
/.gemini/
/.github/
/.agents/
/.vsdlc/scripts/
# --- BMAD module workspace (framework-managed — see the carve-out below) -
/_bmad/*
# --- team-committable BMAD customizations (R11) -------------------------
# Deny-all, then allow-list — order matters, last match wins.
# Docs → How-To Guides → Customizing BMAD skills.
!/_bmad/custom/
/_bmad/custom/*
!/_bmad/custom/.gitignore
!/_bmad/custom/*.toml
/_bmad/custom/*.user.toml
!/_bmad/custom/_shared/
/_bmad-vention/
/_bmad-output/.cache/
/_bmad-output/**/*.lock
/.playwright-cli/
/.playwright/
# --- scratch / OS noise -------------------------------------------------
# transient BMAD custom-source mirror (removed in `finally`; ignored on crash)
/.vsdlc-bmad-src-*/
*.log
.DS_Store
*.tmp
*.bak
# VENTION-SDLC-MANAGED:END
